# Binary assets must never be line-ending "normalized" or diffed as text. Git's
# content detection already gets these right, but naming them explicitly means a
# future tool — or a future asset with a text-like first block — cannot mangle
# them.
#
# No `eol=` rule is imposed on text files on purpose. The scripts are
# line-ending agnostic: `build-kit.mjs` compares generated modules modulo CRLF,
# `link-into-profile.mjs` preserves whatever ending the profile file already
# uses, and the pnpm-workspace rewrite tolerates both. So a Windows checkout with
# the default `core.autocrlf=true` and a macOS/Linux checkout with LF both work,
# and nobody has to renormalize the tree.
*.wav   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.flac  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.tgz   binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
